  "safety_constraints": [
    "Never infer AUTO from missing fields, truthiness, promotion titles, or historical membership.",
    "Joined products: add_mode is the string enum AUTO or SELLER. Only explicit AUTO is eligible.",
    "Future list: snapshot add_mode is boolean, true means manually added; the official article instead names is_manually_added. Only explicit false without contradictory manual signals can qualify. Missing, unknown or conflicting signals remain untouched.",
    "Take exact auto_add_dates from GET /v1/actions for each action/date pair. Do not substitute today or the promotion start date.",
    "Collect every offset page before deleting; verify the same action/date afterward. Do not paginate by increasing offset over a mutating list.",
    "V2 response products, last_id, total and product_ids are root fields; do not assume a v1 result wrapper.",
    "Product_id, id and sku are separate identifiers. Product_ids deletion refers to Ozon product_id.",
    "Money fields are objects. Do not coerce objects with Number or infer RUB when currency is missing.",
    "Changing only the deactivate URL to v2 is not a valid non-voucher Boosting exit strategy.",
    "Strictly greater is the consistent exit condition in the migration guide and update field description; another description says greater-or-equal. Do not use ambiguous equality.",
    "Products/update changes the shared product-card limit and may affect manual participation or other promotions. The 2026-10-27 repair policy is documented in promotions.md: verified automatic-only enrollment, fresh cross-activity manual protection, smallest supported amount strictly above the verified threshold, and no lowering of any known or attempted shared limit.",
    "The guide mentions deferred price changes under auto-add delete although that request has no price. Future-list deletion is a distinct workflow; do not claim it removes already joined products."
  ],
